validate/linked_decay.jl — running log (2026-11-14). Hypotheses are written before each test.
Criteria: validate/linked_decay_criteria.md (committed 02d4c3b before any comparison).

== 0. Derivation (before any kernel comparison) ==

Quantity: C_l = Cov(g_rest, d_l²) at the chromosome level (cis), split over classes s of partner
loci: T_s = κ(B_s, x_l, x_l). The genic accounting's within-locus term is 2βΣ_l(κ3_l + C_l).

One generation, first order in β (regression of π/π̄ on g) and 1/S_c, S_c = ω² + V_E + Var(G_chr)
(the width of E[π | one chromosome] for a Gaussian homolog):
  selection   ΔT_s = β κ(B_s, l, l, G) − [c_s (κ3_l + C_l) + 2κ(l,G) κ(B_s, l, G)]/S_c − κ₅/(2S_c)
              (first-order cumulant change κ(A, log w), Leonov–Shiryaev for the u² term);
              β κ(B_s, l, l, G) = β[K_s + K3_s], K_s = κ(B_s, B, l, l), K3_s = κ(B_s, l, l, l);
  survival    E[T] × (1 − 3/(2n) + 3/(2N))   (subset of n of N; exact enumeration);
  gametes     T × (1 − ρ_s)                   (single crossover; the split pairs are independent);
  offspring   E[T] × (1 − 1/(2N))(1 − 2/(2N)) (2N iid draws);
  mutation    E[ΔT] = 0.
The source: under sampling from a population with x_l independent of its background,
E[K̂] = −2E[ŷ_s Ŷ] exactly (no variance heterogeneity and no three-locus part is seeded), so to
leading order in 1/n, K_s = −2E[y_s Y_l], y_s = Cov(B_s, x_l), the drift-seeded allele–background LD:
  y_s ← f₁(1 − ρ_s)[y_s − (c_s(v_l + Y_l) + v_l y_s)/S_c] + noise, Var(noise) = v_l Var(B_s)/(2n) (+ mutation's).
Decay rates: association ρ_s + 3/(2n) + Cov(B,G)/S_c (the last shared across classes through
C_l); its source ρ_s + 1/(2n) + Cov(B,G)/S_c. Directional selection does not enter the decay at
this order (it enters as the source β). Steady state: per locus 2βC_l = −β² v_l Σ_s V_s/(n(ρ_s+δ_y)(ρ_s+δ_T));
with δ_y = δ_T = δ and V_chr = V_G/2 this is Barton's (1995) excess drift loss, so Barton's term is
the steady state; the kernel starts it from zero at the move. Compared with the spectrum's δ =
1/(2n) + V_G/S: the selection part is the chromosome-level background variance over S_c, about
V_G/(2S) (less where Bulmer LD lowers Var(G_chr)), i.e. about half or less.

Symbolics: validate/symbolic/check_linked_decay.jl, 76 checks PASS.

== 1. Development (set D, R = 3; same runs as genic_decline's runs 1–3) ==

Hypotheses before looking:
  H1  measured K ≈ −2 measured yY (ratio 0.75–1.33) before and during the move.
  H2  the y recursion (drift-seeded LD) predicts Σ yY within a factor 1.5.
  P1  level A with the derived decay predicts ΣC within ±0.2 (log) in 25..199 and beats the
      no-selection and spectrum-δ comparators (expected: :nosel too negative, accumulates too
      long; :spectrum too weak, decays too fast).
  P2  level B predicts ΣC and the cumulative sign-symmetric loss within ±0.3 (log).
  Cross-check: this study's 2β₂ΣC_sym ≈ genic_decline's sym3 on the same runs (differences:
  chromosome vs individual level, trans terms, sampling noise).

