Development reading:
  P1 (decay rate) holds on D: level A with the derived recursion is within +0.06/+0.05/+0.17 (log)
     of the measured ΣC in 25..49/50..99/100..199 (median |.| 0.07/0.05/0.24, 11 eligible inputs);
     without the selection term it is too strong (+0.27/+0.37/+0.53: the association persists too
     long), with the spectrum's δ far too weak (−0.90/−1.41/−1.95).
  H1 fails on D: measured K is only 0.59 (pre-move) to 0.38 (100..199) of −2yY. The parts of K that
     the leading-order closure drops (variance heterogeneity μ(B_s,B,l,l) − Cov(B_s,B)v_l and
     three-locus terms) are positive, about half of −2yY, and grow under the move.
  H2 fails on D: the y recursion gives 0.59–0.76 of the measured Σ yY.
  P2 fails on D: level B overpredicts (+0.23, +0.50, +1.33; cumulative loss +0.48), because its
     source −2E[yY] does not decline under the move as the measured K does.
  Cross-check: 2β₂ΣC_sym (chromosome level) equals genic_decline's sym3 on the same runs to within
     a few per cent in every run.

Amendment decision (before any confirmation run is analysed): none. The verdict rules stay as
committed; the development failures of H1, H2 and P2 are reported here, not tuned away.

== 2. Exploratory (not a verdict): the derived persistence in the spectrum's linked-selection term ==

Driven by genic_decline's 8 runs per D input (its raw records, read only), the spectrum with
genic_decline's time-dependent linked-selection term (Q_c, R_c from zero at the move) and the
derived persistence of the allele–background LD, λ_c = (1 − ρ_c)(1 − 1/(2n))(1 − V_chr/S_c),
against the default (Barton, δ = 1/(2n) + V_G/S, applied at once).
Hypothesis before running: the derived term lowers genic(+100) toward the kernel; because level B
overpredicts the association (section 1, its source −2E[yY] does not fall under the move), it may
overshoot by +200.

